# skgo

**A SvelteKit backend written in Go.** (pronounced "skaygo")

Developers build a server in Go and serve a SvelteKit app from it: file-based
routing, remote functions, and PageServerLoad / LayoutServerLoad are implemented in
Go. There is no SSR and no JavaScript runtime in production: Go serves the built
client bundle, answers every server request kit's client makes, and in dev proxies
to `vp dev`. `skgo` generates, from `*.remote.go` / `page.server.go` /
`layout.server.go`, the Go `http.Handler`s mounted at exactly the URLs SvelteKit
uses, plus type-safe TypeScript stubs (`*.remote.ts`, `+page.server.ts`) that throw
if ever executed — so a valid response always proves Go answered.

It is not a SvelteKit adapter in the true sense; it replaces all server endpoints
with identical Go implementations. Proof is Playwright tests against the running
Go server, never a deductive proof of the protocol.

We never reimplement kit's client, never build or maintain a JS runtime, and never
claim anything that hasn't been demonstrated running.

## Read this first

**Invoke the `agent-protocol` skill at the start of every session and after any
context compaction.** Worktrees, worklogs, `ephemeral/`, checkpoint commits,
squash-merge PRs, and root-checkout synchronization all come from there.

The brief: `ephemeral/brief/2026-09-05-skgo-vision.md`. The plan:
`ephemeral/plans/2026-09-05-skgo-build-plan.md`. The semantic index over pinned
upstream sources and the junkyard: `ephemeral/semantic-index/README.md` — read
`TAXONOMY.md` there before touching a protocol, the toolchain, or codegen.

## Rules

**This is a Go library.** Write Go. Test with `go test`. Build tooling as Go
commands. JavaScript exists here only where SvelteKit itself requires it — the
thin build adapter, `vite.config.ts`, and the example app's client code. Server
endpoints are never written in JavaScript; generated stubs throw.

**Port, don't reverse-engineer.** Kit 3.0.0-next.25 and devalue are pinned under
`ephemeral/inspiration/reference/`. Copy upstream behavior by direct observation
of that source and port its unit tests. Run a Node kit app only when reading the
code is not enough.

**Build the software.** Not ledgers, sprint files, proof harnesses, adjudication
records, or evidence manifests. Verification is ordinary Go tests and Playwright
against the real binary. Code review fixes real bugs in real scenarios; edge cases
go to GitHub issues.

**Don't narrate.** The worklog is for actionable intelligence only.

## Layout

- `ephemeral/` — tracked working material: brief, plans, worklogs, semantic index.
  Never write to `docs/` without express permission.
- `ephemeral/inspiration/` — gitignored token cache: pinned kit/devalue/sirv/mrmime
  clones, the polytype mirror, and `junkyard/` (an earlier attempt that never
  produced a working server). Mine the junkyard through the semantic index; do not
  resurrect its process.

## SvelteKit facts

Kit 3 breaks most model priors. Read
`ephemeral/semantic-index/sources/kit/docs/kit3-facts.md` before writing SvelteKit
code, and check pinned kit source over any documentation site.
